From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Bharat Dintakurti <bdintakurti@nvidia.com>
Date: Mon, 14 Sep 2026 17:07:15 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] NVIDIA: SAUCE: ACPI: processor_idle: Register shared LPI
 power domains

BugLink: https://bugs.launchpad.net/bugs/2167301

Each processor-container _LPI level describes one shared power domain, but
the FFH state used to enter it is composed along a particular CPU path.
CPUs that reach the same container therefore need to share one genpd
without losing their path-specific firmware entry data.

Use the raw enabled parent states as the identity and state table of a
shared domain. Retain each CPU's composed FFH state and wake latency in a
separate runtime map keyed by domain and state index. A later validation
step can commit conservative latency bounds only for complete, usable
paths.

One ACPI container maps to one shared genpd, so CPUs sharing that container
must derive the same EnableParentState-filtered parent-state array. If a
second CPU derives an incompatible array, reject that CPU's hierarchy and
roll it back to the direct flat LPI path.

Journal newly created domains so a failed extraction can remove them
without disturbing domains already used by another CPU. The domains are not
linked and have no CPU consumers yet, and idle entry remains on the direct
path.

